IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 10643 of 2020
CITATION: (2020) 8 SCC 531
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: R.F. Nariman, Surya Kant, V. Ramasubramanian

PARTIES:
CoC Essar Steel vs Satish Kumar Gupta

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 30 IBC, Section 31 IBC

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
commercial wisdom of coc, adjudicating authority review, clean slate principle

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Reiterated primacy of commercial wisdom of the Committee of Creditors, limiting NCLT/NCLAT jurisdiction to procedural review without substituting business judgment.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 30 IBC, Section 31 IBC.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

